  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-03-28T14:40:02.536Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Noticed that my profile is still visible to users I block. This is so unsafe. It can and has resulted in stalking and harassment. If a user chooses to, they can search up a user of someone who has blocked them and keep tabs, find them on alt accounts, possibly make them an ongoing target. All because they can still access the profile info. Not the best feeling knowing my socials and linked domains are not safe in my profile from potentially malicious people that I block. Maybe only allow group instance owners and mods to see the profiles of those who block them? For the sake of their instance moderation I can understand that. But to keep everything 100% public to blocked users is dangerous. Perhaps remove only bio, links, status, user notes and badges? They can still search but their access to the profile is extremely limited.",
